# Deploy API to GKE

## GKE Cluster
- Cluster: `autopilot-cluster-tradar` (us-west1)
- Namespace: `x402-xrpl`
- External IP: `35.247.41.7`
- Image: `us-west1-docker.pkg.dev/tworld-473700/x402-xrpl/api:latest`

## Deploy Steps

1. Connect to cluster:
```bash
gcloud container clusters get-credentials autopilot-cluster-tradar --region us-west1
```

2. Build AMD64 image and push (from repo root):
```bash
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 -f apps/api/Dockerfile \
  -t us-west1-docker.pkg.dev/tworld-473700/x402-xrpl/api:latest --push .
```

3. Restart pods to pull new image:
```bash
kubectl rollout restart deployment/x402-api -n x402-xrpl
```

4. Check status:
```bash
kubectl get pods -n x402-xrpl
kubectl logs -n x402-xrpl -l app=x402-api --tail=20
curl http://35.247.41.7/health
```

## Important Notes
- MUST build with `--platform linux/amd64` (Mac is ARM, GKE is AMD64)
- Uses `node:20-slim` (Debian), NOT Alpine (Prisma needs glibc + OpenSSL)
- Database credentials stored in K8s secret `api-secrets` in `x402-xrpl` namespace
- Database uses private IP `10.77.97.16` (same VPC as GKE)
- K8s manifest: `k8s/api-deployment.yaml`
